<Base
  title="About"
  description="About Vish Vaddi — estimator, writer, builder."
>
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p>
    I'm Vish. I live in Sydney, work as a senior estimator in retail fitout,
    and spend the rest of my time reading, writing, training, and building
    software I want to exist.
  </p>

  <h2>Professional</h2>
  <p>
    I price construction work — tenders for shopfitters, fitout contractors,
    and retail and hospitality clients. The work is half maths, half judgement,
    and increasingly half AI tooling I build myself. The CV-shaped version is
    at <a href="/work">/work</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Personal</h2>
  <p>
    I take notes constantly. Atomic ideas, lessons from tenders won and lost,
    things I've changed my mind about. The most durable ones land at
    <a href="/notes">/notes</a>. The system underneath is an Obsidian vault
    inspired by <a href="https://stephango.com/">Steph Ango</a>'s
    file-over-app philosophy: plain markdown on disk, no platform lock-in,
    links over folders.
  </p>

  <h2>What I read</h2>
  <p>
    A rotating mix of decision science (Taleb, Annie Duke, Adam Grant), the
    Stoics (Marcus, Epictetus), Indian philosophy (the Bhagavad Gita, Vedanta),
    construction industry writing, and whatever recent biology and sleep
    research is shifting how I train and recover.
  </p>

  <h2>What I build</h2>
  <p>
    A small portfolio of side projects, most useful to me first: scope-generation
    tooling for estimators, a roguelike submarine game, a portable AI assistant
    for construction sites. The point of side projects is that the process is
    the product.
  </p>

  <h2>Find me</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Email — <a href="mailto:vishvaddi@gmail.com">vishvaddi@gmail.com</a></li>
    <li>GitHub — <a href="https://github.com/vishvaddi">github.com/vishvaddi</a></li>
  </ul>

